Finding the max/min value in an array of primitives using Java It's trivial to write a function to determine the min/max value in an array, such as: /**
 * 
 * @param chars
 * @return the max value in the array of chars
 */
private static int maxValue(char[] chars) {
    int max = chars[0];
    for (int ktr = 0; ktr < chars.length; ktr++) {
        if (chars[ktr] > max) {
            max = chars[ktr];
        }
    }
    return max;
} but isn't this already done somewhere?

